pairs.good:
Track what you've seen in a set and return the index the first time a value repeats. O(n) time, O(n) space.

```python
def first_duplicate_index(nums):
    seen = set()
    for i, x in enumerate(nums):
        if x in seen:
            return i
        seen.add(x)
    return -1
```

pairs.bad:
Use a set so it's O(n): return the first repeated value as soon as you see it.

```python
def first_duplicate_index(nums):
    for i in range(len(nums)):
        for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)):
            if nums[i] == nums[j]:
                return nums[i]
    return -1
```
